New: Make the variable-coefficient INS integrators read bdry_interp_type ("LINEAR" or "QUADRATIC") and pass their boundary treatment to the Stokes operator and preconditioner, the velocity and pressure subdomain solvers, the divergence-free velocity extension, and the velocity boundary conditions, including the TRACTION value of IBAMR::INSVCStaggeredVelocityBcCoef beyond a corner with a velocity boundary, and use it in their own velocity fills, so that the explicit and implicit viscous terms use the same treatment. Overrides, errors, and the plog report of differing treatments are as in IBAMR::INSStaggeredHierarchyIntegrator. IBAMR::VCStaggeredStokesProjectionPreconditioner and IBTK::VCSCViscousOperator use the extrapolation type of the boundary treatment. The plog report includes the mass and momentum integrator of the conservative form.
